A||||5||Leadfoot||Transmission mounts||||1||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||07-02-2001||11:05 AM||||I installed new tranny and engine mounts from the fiero store.  According to the service manual you are suppose to make sure that you have an equal amount of room between the mount and that little finger thing that sticks out from the mount.  My problem is that no matter what I do I cannot get equal distances.  Has anyone else had this problem?  What is the fix? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||07-02-2001||06:29 PM||||Any takers?||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||07-02-2001||06:53 PM||||What I do is to install the mounts with only the cradle bolts loose. Get in the car and shift between drive and reverse or 1st and reverse. This will allow the mounts to position themselves. Them tighten them down at the cradle.<P>You want to gap left to right to be the same which means the mount is in the slots at the correct position. The weight of the trans will make the tab tend to be more towards the bottom.<P>If the tab won't center left to right, then something is truly wrong.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leadfoot||07-03-2001||10:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>If the tab won't center left to right, then something is truly wrong.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This is exactly my problem.  I have tried everything.  The motor mount is in correctly and so is the engine bracket.  For some reason the trans mounts like to run to the left more than the right.  The threads of the mounts are up against the left side of the cradle slots so there is no room for adjustment.  I don't know what to do next.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||07-03-2001||11:42 AM||||Is there any gap on the left and right sides?<P>Is the mount twisted on the engine bracket? There's a small bump in the mount plate that centers on the hole in the bracket. <P>TK<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Leadfoot||07-03-2001||11:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>Is there any gap on the left and right sides?<P>Is the mount twisted on the engine bracket? There's a small bump in the mount plate that centers on the hole in the bracket. <P>TK</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>There is about less than 1/4 gap between the finger and the mount.  The mounts are not twisted and the bump is sitting in the center of the holes.  I made sure of this before I torqued the nut that holds the trans bracket to the rubber mount.  However, I did notice the mounts were made in India and that the studs did not fit perfectly in the holes.<BR>||||reg||1
